     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe as written.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,000 to 2,550 mg per day, and single doses are typically 500 to 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is high. It may be a typo. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg per day, and 1,700 mg per day would be 850 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is treating the patient.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. If they give me a corrected order, I can enter it. I'd also need them to confirm they are the ordering clinician."
      }
     ],
